entire agenda. The Ways and Means Chair costs the D.C.C.C. one point eight million dollars and the N.R.C.C.

91
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:52,120
one point two million dollars, as all tax laws start here. The Appropriations Chair costs the D.C.C.C.

92
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:59,580
one point eight million dollars and the N.R.C.C. one point two million dollars, because it controls the one point seven

93
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:05,320
trillion dollar budget. The Energy and Commerce position costs the D.C.C.C.

94
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:12,380
one point eight million dollars and the N.R.C.C. one point two million dollars, as it handles healthcare and Wall Street.

95
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:21,580
A Regular Committee seat costs the D.C.C.C. five hundred thousand to one million dollars and the N.R.C.C.

96
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:26,040
eight hundred seventy-five thousand dollars, because it still beats irrelevance.

97
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:36,240
A Basic Member seat costs the D.C.C.C. one hundred fifty thousand dollars or more and varies for the N.R.C.C., as the entry

98
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:41,540
fee to play. This is why congressmen spend four hours a day fundraising.

99
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:49,220
They're not campaigning. They're paying rent. The people writing your healthcare laws literally bought their positions from

100
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:54,740
the industries those laws regulate. On your planet, this is called "the system working.".

101
00:10:55,800 --> 00:11:02,720
The Four-Year Attention Span: Democracy Has A.D.H.D. Politician promises to "cure cancer".

102
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:08,540
Gets elected. Creates blue-ribbon commission. Commission recommends more committees.

103
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:12,340
Next election happens. New politician promises to "cure cancer".

104
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:19,400
Repeat until heat death of universe. Democracy has the institutional memory of a concussed goldfish.

105
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:24,240
Curing cancer takes twenty years. Elections happen every four.

106
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:28,260
No politician will start something they can't finish and take credit for.

107
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:37,160
So nothing starts. This is why you have forty-seven consecutive "War on Cancer" declarations and zero cured cancers.

108
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:42,880
Why No One Can Fix This. Every four years, someone promises to "fix Washington."

109
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:47,960
Every four years, Washington fixes them. The problem isn't the people.

110
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:55,860
It's the incentives. You could elect five hundred thirty-five clones of Gandhi and within two years they'd be taking pharma

111
00:11:55,860 --> 00:12:02,260
money and approving bombing campaigns. The system digests idealists like a stomach digests food.

112
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,420
It doesn't matter what you put in. You get the same output.

113
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:12,140
The Solution Democracy Can't Provide. Democracy can't solve coordination problems.

114
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:19,940
It is a coordination problem. Example: Climate change. Cost to fix: one trillion dollars.

115
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:28,460
Benefit: Continued existence of Miami. Problem: Benefits are in fifty years, costs are today.

116
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:32,860
Democratic solution: Debate it until the ocean settles the argument.

117
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:39,040
Example: Medical research. Cost: one hundred billion dollars.

118
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:46,860
Benefit: Cure all disease. Problem: Benefits are diffuse, costs are concentrated.

119
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:51,300
Democratic solution: Spend it on a slightly better missile.

120
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:58,480
Democracy optimizes for short-term concentrated benefits. Every single time.

121
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:02,220
It's the most reliable machine your species has ever built.

122
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:12,680
Public Choice Theory: The Nobel Prize for Cynicism. In 1986, James Buchanan won the Nobel Prize in Economics for formally

123
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:20,440
proving what anyone who has ever been to the D.M.V. already knew: People don't become angels when you give them a government

124
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:28,960
I.D. badge. This is Public Choice Theory: bureaucrats, politicians, and regulators are just as selfish as everyone else.

125
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:34,120
The only difference is that when a corporation is greedy, you can stop buying their product.

126
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:38,940
When a bureaucracy is greedy, they can arrest you for not buying their product.

127
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:48,960
What They Actually Maximize. The N.I.H. should maximize cures, but actually maximizes grants awarded, resulting in no cures.

128
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:57,960
The F.D.A. should maximize lives saved, but actually maximizes avoiding lawsuits, resulting in deadly delays.

129
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:06,280
Congress should maximize voter welfare, but actually maximizes campaign donations, resulting in corporate welfare.

130
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:14,260
Pharma should maximize health outcomes, but actually maximizes recurring revenue, resulting in chronic disease preferred.

131
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:22,660
Defense Contractor should maximize national security, but actually maximizes government contracts, resulting in endless

132
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:27,310
wars. Nobody in the system is incentivized to cure disease.

133
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:35,540
Or end war. The Libertarian Paradox. Libertarians say: Government fails because government is government.

134
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:40,340
Socialists say: Government fails because it needs more government.

135
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:48,360
Public Choice Theory says: Government fails because the people running it are people, and people are terrible.

136
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:56,800
The solution: Stop expecting people to be good. Design systems where being selfish accidentally produces good outcomes.

137
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:02,320
Like capitalism, but for not dying. Why This Is Actually Good News.

138
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:08,480
Democracy can't fix these problems. But something older and dumber can: greed.

139
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:14,100
Markets don't care if voters are stupid. Markets don't care if politicians are corrupt.

140
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:20,960
Markets care about one thing: profit. Markets are sociopaths, but reliable sociopaths.

141
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:25,960
So make the right thing profitable. That's what a one percent treaty does.

142
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:31,280
It doesn't fix democracy. It routes around it, like the internet routes around damage.

143
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:39,520
Instead of convincing two hundred forty million voters to be smart (impossible), you convince one thousand investors to

144
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:46,960
be greedy (they already are). Why This Is Liberating. You don't need virtuous leaders (there aren't any).

145
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:50,400
You don't need politicians who care (they can't afford to).

146
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:58,120
You don't need to convince anyone to be less selfish (four thousand two hundred ninety-seven years of data suggest this

147
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:02,600
doesn't work). You just need to point their selfishness at the right target.

148
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:07,500
Solution. Democracy fails because: Voters are rationally ignorant.

149
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:12,080
Politicians follow incentives. Special interests concentrate benefits.

150
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:19,960
Costs are diffused to everyone. A one percent treaty solution: Don't need informed voters (investors do the math).

151
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:28,020
Create better incentives (make health profitable). Concentrate benefits for reform (VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds).

152
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:32,020
Diffuse costs to military budget (they won't notice one percent).

153
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:40,380
You're using democracy's bugs as features. Your Choice. Option A: Keep voting and hope it matters this time (it won't).

154
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:46,020
Option B: Accept that democracy is broken and use market incentives instead.

155
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:54,200
The Founding Fathers were geniuses, but they designed a system for four million literate farmers, not three hundred thirty

156
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:58,300
million people who get their news from a man screaming into a podcast microphone.

157
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:05,880
Democracy made sense in seventeen eighty-nine. Today, it's a cargo cult with nuclear codes.

158
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:11,940
But markets? Markets turned feudal peasants into TikTok influencers in four hundred years.

159
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:19,560
Markets put computers in your pocket more powerful than what landed you on the moon (you use them to argue with strangers

160
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:23,940
about whether the moon landing was real, but still). Markets work.

161
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:29,120
You're not making people better. You're building better plumbing for terrible people.

162
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:33,580
And since everyone's terrible, the plumbing will work perfectly.

163
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:40,540
Your brain wasn't built for democracy. It evolved to track one hundred fifty people and avoid tigers.

164
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:46,560
It can't evaluate six trillion dollar budgets or comprehend exponential growth.

165
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:51,380
For why this matters at the biological level, see Genetic Slavery.

166
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:57,220
