in Washington. Half of them used to work in the government they're now bribing, which on your planet is called "a career

169
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:19,560
path" rather than "corruption." In twenty twenty-three, corporations spent four point one billion dollars on lobbying.

170
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:26,740
That's seven point seven million dollars per congressman who makes one hundred seventy-four thousand dollars a year.

171
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:34,580
Each congressman is surrounded by seven point seven million dollars worth of professional persuasion and earns less than

172
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:38,160
a mid-level dentist. The mystery is not that they're corrupt.

173
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:45,880
The mystery is that any of them aren't. Citizens United made corporations people who can donate unlimited money through

174
