183
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:46,460
Pharma employs 3 lobbyists for every member of Congress. The F.D.A.

184
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:51,440
gets seventy-five percent of its drug review budget from the companies it regulates.

185
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:56,880
For the full accounting, see Cost of War and F.D.A.: Unsafe and Ineffective.

186
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:05,380
The system maintains itself with the elegant efficiency of a parasite that keeps its host alive just enough to keep feeding.

187
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:10,180
Cures are a one-time payment; treatments are recurring revenue.

188
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:17,440
Approving a bad drug ends careers; delaying a good one ends lives (but not careers, and careers are what matter to people

189
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:22,500
with careers). Everyone who matters wins. Everyone who's dying loses.

190
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:27,280
The system works perfectly. It's just optimized for the wrong thing.

191
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:35,380
The Solution They Don't Want. The whole system runs on one trick: each American loses one hundred dollars to corruption

192
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:43,260
(not worth a phone call). Each corporation gains one hundred million dollars (worth a thousand phone calls, a lobbyist army,

193
